    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "06eadd94_5a32ade4",
        "filename": "common/charge_state_v2.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1465,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106416
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-21T12:04:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not \"mode\" ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1465,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1465,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "f35873a4cb88a1d03af5965d4b5b1876525e94d8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "328d4132_de819013",
        "filename": "common/charge_state_v2.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1465,
      "author": {
        "id": 1444467
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-22T02:06:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since `is_chg_ctrl_mode_idle_disabled` is defined as the variable to check if the extra control has been carried out. If we are up to set charge control idle, at this moment, `mode` should be CHARGE_CONTROL_IDLE. `chg_ctl_mode` stands for the mode before we set to idle mode, which means that it is not CHARGE_CONTROL_IDLE if we did not set it to idle mode and the extra control has not been carried out.",
      "parentUuid": "06eadd94_5a32ade4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1465,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1465,
        "endChar": 17
      },
